            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="1122" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v09/pg1079"/>

                <head>299. Message From the Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and
                    Pacific Affairs (Sullivan) to the President’s Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d299-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Paris</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1973-01-18T22:11:00+00:00">January 18, 1973,
                        2211Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item> Thach has proposed that January 19 be our last day of negotiations this
                        week. He wishes use all available language experts for conformity of texts
                        on Saturday and Sunday.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d299-f2"/> In fact, today, we
                        negotiated in French, not a totally satisfactory exercise, because language
                        experts at work.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>He feels that, if we can not rpt not solve entry point issue January 19,
                        we should wait for Monday. It is not rpt not clear whether this is pressure
                        tactic, or whether, as he claims, he as yet unable nominate proposed
                        seaports. If latter is case, it may be that he wishes minimize time between
                        their nomination and the cease-fire in order preclude preemptive seizure by
                        ARVN.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In any event, I saw no choice but to accept his proposal, especially since
                        January 20 is scheduled to be day of massive demonstrations, which may
                        immobilize Embassy, including its garage.</item>
                    <pb facs="1123" n="1080" xml:id="pg1080"/>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Given this situation, I have accepted invitation to spend Saturday and
                        Sunday with friends in St. Moritz. Aldrich will remain here to nurse his
                        cold and work with language experts. Unless you have sadistic desire to
                        confine me to Paris, which you express before I buy my tickets morning
                        January 19, I shall take this breather. Before leaving, I will provide
                        telephone number where I can be reached.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>Warm regards.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d299-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d299-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Kissinger
                    Office Files, Box 119, Country Files, Far East, Vietnam Negotiations, Ambassador
                    Porter’s File—Paris, June 1972–January 1973. Secret; Sensitive; Exclusively Eyes
